ana: Pushed PR to add a Go SDK snippet for quota-aware retries, update a couple of stale Grafana links on the Quotas page, and add a tiny migration note for v1.12 -> v1.13. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/8348

peter: Thanks  can you summarize the Go example? We currently don't have any Go docs for handling quota headers.

ana: (typo) ana: Sure. The snippet shows resilient header lookup across aliases (X-RW-Quota, X-Quota-Cap, X-Rate-Limit) and returns a normalized struct {Value int, Unit string}. I also included a short backoff example that uses the header to cap retries. Paste from PR: 

```go
// Go SDK: read quota header with fallback and normalize
func ParseQuota(h http.Header) (int, string) {
    candidates := []string{"X-RW-Quota", "X-Quota-Cap", "X-Rate-Limit"}
    for _, k := range candidates {
        if v := h.Get(k); v != "" {
            digits := regexp.MustCompile("\\d+").FindString(v)
            if digits == "" { return 0, "minute" }
            return strconv.Atoi(digits)
        }
    }
    return 0, "minute"
}
```

